language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ cell_tower: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A telecom company needs to build a set of cell towers to provide signal coverage for the inhabitants of a city. A number of potential locations where the towers could be built have been identified, and the towers have a fixed range. Due to budget constraints only a limited number of them can be built. The city is split into regions, each with a known population. Choose which of the potential locations to build cell towers on so as to provide coverage to as many people as possible.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `cell_tower.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/cell_tower.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `cell_tower_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py cell_tower.json
$   savilerow model.eprime cell_tower_1.param -run-solver

$ number of potential tower sites, derived from the data: the length of cost (not a field of the reader's JSON)
given cost_dim1 : int(1..)
$ number of regions, derived from the data: the length of population (not a field of the reader's JSON)
given population_dim1 : int(1..)
$ budget: the total cost of the towers that can be built
given budget : int
$ cost[i]: cost of building a tower at site i, indices 1-based
given cost : matrix indexed by [int(1..cost_dim1)] of int
$ population[j]: population of region j, indices 1-based
given population : matrix indexed by [int(1..population_dim1)] of int
$ delta[i,j]: 1 if a tower at site i covers region j, 0 otherwise, indices 1-based (sites by regions)
given delta : matrix indexed by [int(1..cost_dim1), int(1..population_dim1)] of int(0..1)

$ build_tower[i]: a tower is built at site i
find build_tower : matrix indexed by [int(1..cost_dim1)] of bool
$ covered[j]: region j is covered by at least one tower built (auxiliary: only the implication is needed, since the population covered is maximised)
find covered : matrix indexed by [int(1..population_dim1)] of bool
$ total_population_covered: the total population of the covered regions
find total_population_covered : int(0..(sum j : int(1..population_dim1) . population[j]))

maximising total_population_covered
such that
$ the total cost of the towers built does not exceed the budget
(sum i : int(1..cost_dim1) . toInt(build_tower[i]) * cost[i]) <= budget,
$ a region is covered only if some tower built at a site that covers it
forAll j : int(1..population_dim1) . covered[j] -> exists i : int(1..cost_dim1) . (build_tower[i] /\ delta[i,j] = 1),
$ the total population covered is the sum of the populations of the covered regions
total_population_covered = (sum j : int(1..population_dim1) . toInt(covered[j]) * population[j])
